      "documentConcept": "Mitochondrial and mitophagy targets: PINK1, parkin, USP30",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:40bf692086d85e7a6b125921c155d79d1c276cc4368bc06ef076be7551b42911",
      "text": "PINK1 (a ubiquitin kinase) and parkin (an E3 ligase) flag damaged mitochondria for mitophagy, and mutations in both are linked to autosomal recessive PD. USP30, a mitochondrial deubiquitinase, opposes this pathway. Preclinical mouse and human-neuron studies support USP30 inhibition; Mission Therapeutics reports its USP30 inhibitor MTX325 has reached patients with PD in a Phase 1b study. PINK1 activators such as MTK458 are earlier-stage, and a Science Advances paper reports PINK1/Parkin-independent off-target effects for two activators.",
